; fas9_underlays.scr - facit script of step 9.6 (F9.3 underlays: PDFUNDERLAY/PDFDEFINITION, DWFUNDERLAY/DWFDEFINITION,
; DGNUNDERLAY/DGNDEFINITION). Run it with
;   python -I tools/fas9_prune_entities.py build/test-data/acadsharp/sample_AC1032_ascii.dxf build/fas9_underlays_input.dxf PDFUNDERLAY VIEWPORT 3DSOLID REGION MESH
;   python -I tools/fas9_facit_run.py doc/facit/fas9_underlays.scr --input build/fas9_underlays_input.dxf
; The drawing it starts from is ACadSharp's sample_AC1032_ascii.dxf (an AutoCAD 2018 file, test/data/manifest.cmake) with every entity
; but its PDFUNDERLAY (handle D07, one definition D06 `..\pdf-definition.pdf`, page 1, insertion 16.2869,15) removed, so a point pick
; at 16.2869,15 is the underlay alone. AutoCAD 2025's core reads that file and saves it in every version it can, so the records are
; AutoCAD's own.
;
; What AutoCAD 2025's core cannot do, and what is therefore "ej testat" (plan 2026-10-27-fas-9-typer.md, F9.3):
;   -PDFATTACH, -DWFATTACH, -DGNATTACH (and PDFATTACH/DWFATTACH/DGNATTACH, with FILEDIA 0 or 1): the core ends with an access violation
;     (exit code 0xC0000005) as soon as the command starts, with or without a file name, also after ARX-loading AcDgnUI.crx; so
;     no DWFUNDERLAY/DWFDEFINITION/DGNUNDERLAY/DGNDEFINITION is ever made, and the PDF underlay is not a fresh attachment of a real
;     PDF but the sample's (its file `pdf-definition.pdf` is not there: "Underlay Definition Corner Points:" is empty).
;   -PDFCLIP, -DWFCLIP, -DGNCLIP (unknown commands in the core): rectangle/polygon clip, inside/outside clip and the clip's 11/21
;     points are not made; the sample's flags are 280 = 3 (clipping on, underlay on) with no boundary.
;   DWF/DGN source files (EXPORTDWF and -DGNEXPORT give nothing without a display), and a real PDF page outline for the
;     proxy graphics (the plotted PDF `src_a.pdf` of -PLOT "DWG To PDF.pc3" works but cannot be attached, see above).
;   An underlay in paper space: COPYTOLAYOUT is not in the core and CHSPACE ends it with an access violation (the
;     underlay's own paper space cannot be made); a block's INSERT (-BLOCK, -INSERT) works and is below.
; Plain AutoCAD commands, no LISP. ;SAVE saves R12, 2000, 2004, 2007, 2010, 2013 and 2018, ASCII and binary.
;EXPECT PDFUNDERLAY PDFDEFINITION
;SAVE underlay_pdf
; A second instance that shares the definition
_.COPY
16.2869,15

0,0
100,50
;SAVE underlay_pdf copied
; Rotation of the first instance (50), then a scale (41/42/43), then a normal other than Z (210)
_.ROTATE
16.2869,15

16.2869,15
30
;SAVE underlay_pdf rotated
_.SCALE
16.2869,15

16.2869,15
2
;SAVE underlay_pdf scaled
_.ROTATE3D
16.2869,15

_X
16.2869,15,0
90
;SAVE underlay_pdf normal
; Mirror of the second instance (the source is erased: the mirrored one stands at x 300 - 116.2869)
_.MIRROR
116.2869,65

150,0
150,10
_Y
;SAVE underlay_pdf mirrored
; Erase one instance: the definition (and its dictionary entry) stays for the other
_.ERASE
183.7131,65

;SAVE underlay_pdf instance_erased
; The last instance goes into a block, which is inserted scaled by 2 and turned 45 degrees: the underlay is the block's entity,
; the INSERT carries the transform
_.-BLOCK
ULBLK
0,0,0
16.2869,15

_.-INSERT
ULBLK
200,0,0
2
2
45
;SAVE underlay_pdf in_block
; Erase the INSERT, then purge: what AutoCAD does with the definition and ACAD_PDFDEFINITIONS
_.ERASE
_L

;SAVE underlay_pdf all_erased
_.-PURGE
_A
*
_N
;SAVE underlay_pdf purged
